2025-12-24 01:35:12 | INFO | Q235 id=GJ6r_T6ckc4_00-00-00_00-00-06 | baseline_pred=A | gold=C | prompt_variant=medium | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=The audio provided consists of a sequence of short and long beeps, which is characteristic of Morse code.\n\nThe sequence of beeps is:\nShort-Short-Short (dot-dot-dot)\nLong-Long-Long (dash-dash-dash)\nShort-Short-Short (dot-dot-dot)\n\nIn International Morse Code:\n*   Three short signals ($\cdot\cdot\cdot$) represent the letter 'S'.\n*   Three long signals (---) represent the letter 'O'.\n\nTherefore, the sequence $\cdot\cdot\cdot$ --- $\cdot\cdot\cdot$ decodes to "SOS".\n\nComparing this to the choices:\nA) sOS\nB) cODE\nC) hELLO\nD) wORLD\n\nThe information encoded is SOS.\n\nAnswer: $\boxed{A}$
