ontrol of the physical situation at that moment, potentially having hit or taken Parker down.\n\nLet's re-evaluate the sequence:\n*   "Take the picture, Parker. Put him down, Flash." (Parker is told to put someone down)\n*   "Take the picture. Put him down, Eugene!" (Eugene is told to put someone down)\n*   "Come on, get up, Parker!" (Parker is down)\n*   "Stay down, Parker!" (Parker is being told to remain down)\n\nThe most direct evidence of who is physically dominant or who caused the current state comes from the commands directed at the individuals. The command "Put him down, Eugene!" suggests Eugene is in a position of physical control over someone else, or is being told to cease an action that involves putting someone down. The subsequent command "Stay down, Parker!" confirms Parker is the one being subdued. This strongly suggests Eugene was the one who put Parker down.\n\nTherefore, Eugene hit/took down Parker.\n\nAnswer: \boxed{B}
