2025-12-24 02:02:05 | INFO | Q675 id=BV1BPRnYAEx6_00-14-34_00-14-40 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=medium | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=Reason step by step:\n1.  **Analyze the audio information:** The audio states that one steak (牛排) costs "over 50 US dollars" (五十多美元), which is approximately "400 RMB" (大概400人民币).\n2.  **Analyze the cost per person:** The audio then states that if everyone gets one steak ("我们如果一人一份牛排"), the total cost will be "1600 RMB" (就要花掉1600).\n3.  **Calculate the number of people:** To find the number of people, divide the total cost by the cost per person:\n    $$\text{Number of people} = \frac{\text{Total Cost}}{\text{Cost per person}}$$\n    $$\text{Number of people} = \frac{1600 \text{ RMB}}{400 \text{ RMB/person}}$$\n    $$\text{Number of people} = 4$$\n4.  **Compare with choices:** The calculated number of people is 4, which corresponds to choice C.\n\nAnswer: \boxed{C}
2025-12-24 02:02:08 | INFO | Q676 id=BV11yrkYME4G_00-03-24_00-03-43 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=medium | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=The user is asking to identify which of the three mentioned acids (nitric acid, hydrochloric acid, or sulfuric acid) has the strongest acidity, based on the provided audio.\n\n**Step-by-step reasoning based on the audio:**\n\n1.  **Identify the acids mentioned and their PK values:** The audio states the PK values for three acids:\n    *   "硝酸的PK是負1.3" (Nitric acid's PK is -1.3).\n    *   "硫酸是負3" (Sulfuric acid is -3).\n    *   "而鹽酸是負7" (And hydrochloric acid is -7).\n\n2.  **Relate PK value to acidity:** In chemistry, for acids, a lower (more negative) $\text{pK}_a$ value indicates a stronger acid (stronger acidity).\n\n3.  **Compare the PK values:**\n    *   Nitric acid ($\text{HNO}_3$): $\text{pK} = -1.3$\n    *   Sulfuric acid ($\text{H}_2\text{SO}_4$): $\text{pK} = -3$\n    *   Hydrochloric acid ($\text{HCl}$): $\text{pK} = -7$\n\n4.  **Determine the strongest acid:** Comparing the values ($-7 < -3 < -1.3$), hydrochloric acid has the lowest (most negative) $\text{pK}$ value, meaning it is the strongest acid among the three mentioned.\n\n5.  **Match with choices:**\n    *   A) sulfurous acid (Not mentioned with a PK value in the comparison)\n    *   B) sulfuric acid ($\text{pK} = -3$)\n    *   C) hydrochloric acid ($\text{pK} = -7$)\n    *   D) nitric acid ($\text{pK} = -1.3$)\n\nThe strongest acid based on the audio data is hydrochloric acid, which corresponds to choice C.\n\nAnswer: $\boxed{C}$
