re used.\nIf we must choose the *best* fit, and Vibrato is undeniably present, an option that omits it is weak. However, since D includes Falsetto (which is likely absent), D is worse than C. Therefore, C, confirming the presence of two distinct techniques (Glissando and Scat), is the most accurate statement among the choices provided, despite the omission of Vibrato.\n\nFinal check: Glissando (slides) and Scat (nonsense syllables) are both clearly audible.\n\nAnswer: $\boxed{C}$
